Satellite records show the Arctic melt season grew longer for decades before it leveled off around 2010.

00:00:49.980 --> 00:00:53.280
The change happened even as overall ice loss continued.

00:00:54.060 --> 00:00:58.660
Researchers tracked start and end dates of each season across many years of data.

