00:01:33.500 --> 00:01:38.180
A new study from the Max Planck Institute for Solar System Research asks whether the

00:01:38.180 --> 00:01:40.280
Sun can only produce modest flares.

00:01:40.920 --> 00:01:46.120
Their analysis shows the Sun shares traits with stars that produce far larger outbursts.

00:01:46.540 --> 00:01:51.200
Historical records contain no direct proof of past superflares on our own star.

00:01:51.200 --> 00:01:56.020
The results revise earlier ideas about the upper limits of solar activity.

00:01:56.720 --> 00:02:03.360
Universe today summarized the paper. Astronomers have tracked a giant planet whose orbit is carrying it out of view.

00:02:03.980 --> 00:02:08.640
The planet shows unusual dynamical behavior that changes its visibility from Earth.

00:02:09.200 --> 00:02:13.480
Ground telescopes recorded its current location before the observing window closes.

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:17.020
The world is expected to stay hidden for a long stretch.

00:02:17.020 --> 00:02:20.480
match. More observations are planned before access ends.

00:02:21.220 --> 00:02:26.700
Eurasia Review reported the tracking work. UC Riverside researchers modeled how Venus

00:02:26.700 --> 00:02:32.540
could have captured and later consumed Iraqi satellite. The planet matches Earth in size

00:02:32.540 --> 00:02:39.080
and mass, yet has no moon today. Their simulations show tidal forces and orbital decay could pull

00:02:39.080 --> 00:02:44.820
a moon inward until it disintegrates. The model explains Venus' slow rotation and thick

00:02:44.820 --> 00:02:51.940
atmosphere. No leftover material has turned up in existing surveys. Fizz.org space carried the study.

00:02:52.660 --> 00:02:58.600
The sun moves through active and quiet phases on an 11-year cycle. A century of data shows

00:02:58.600 --> 00:03:04.400
clear swings in sunspot counts and magnetic strength. Forecasters still struggle to predict the

00:03:04.400 --> 00:03:10.080
exact timing and peak strength of each maximum. The cycle drives space weather that can disrupt

00:03:10.080 --> 00:03:11.180
satellite systems.

00:03:11.860 --> 00:03:15.060
On-going monitoring is steadily improving the forecast models.

00:03:15.800 --> 00:03:18.120
Fizz.org space outline the patterns.

