00:03:54.110 --> 00:03:58.680
The pictures caught the first brightening of a supernova as its shockwave broke out.

00:03:59.240 --> 00:04:02.620
The galaxy sits roughly 75 million light years away.

00:04:02.620 --> 00:04:08.740
Bousso's new camera recorded the event ahead of professional follow-up. The detection ranks among

00:04:08.740 --> 00:04:13.860
the earliest recorded shock breakouts. Astronomy magazine recounted the observation.

