00:06:45.140 --> 00:06:50.800
supplies. Specific project details will follow in coming months. Policy reports summarized

00:06:50.800 --> 00:06:55.360
the pledge. The study on Venus proposes that a captured moon could have been pulled

00:06:55.360 --> 00:07:01.080
inward by tidal forces until it crossed the Roche limit and disintegrated. Fragments

00:07:01.080 --> 00:07:06.380
would then have spiraled into the atmosphere or been vaporized by heat. This mechanism differs

00:07:06.380 --> 00:07:11.700
from Earth's giant impact origin for its moon. The model accounts for Venus's current

00:07:11.700 --> 00:07:17.920
retrograde rotation without requiring an external collision. It remains unclear whether any trace

00:07:17.920 --> 00:07:21.960
of the lost moon persists in the planet's atmosphere or surface composition.

00:07:22.880 --> 00:07:26.900
Future atmospheric probes may yet detect a specific remnant signature.

00:07:27.740 --> 00:07:33.680
The Sun's magnetic field flips polarity roughly every 11 years. Imagine Earth's own magnetic

00:07:33.680 --> 00:07:39.070
poles reversing while you drive from New York to Los Angeles at highway speed. The entire

00:07:39.070 --> 00:07:42.610
Another journey would finish before the sun completes even one full reversal.

00:07:43.350 --> 00:07:47.590
Charged plasma trapped along those field lines builds up tension until it snaps.

00:07:48.510 --> 00:07:52.770
Energy then accelerates particles outward at speeds reaching several hundred kilometers

00:07:52.770 --> 00:07:53.450
per second.

00:07:54.130 --> 00:07:57.970
One such burst carries enough energy to power a major city for weeks.

00:07:58.670 --> 00:08:03.210
The particles must still travel 150 million kilometers before they reach Earth.

00:08:03.210 --> 00:08:09.250
Spacecraft at the Sun Earth L1 point measure the arrival of these particles roughly 40 minutes

00:08:09.250 --> 00:08:11.110
before they strike the upper atmosphere.

00:08:11.530 --> 00:08:16.470
The exact trigger that decides whether a given cycle produces only modest flares or

00:08:16.470 --> 00:08:19.590
a rare super flare still escapes current models.

00:08:20.230 --> 00:08:25.870
We record the timing of every reversal with increasing precision, yet the threshold that separates

00:08:25.870 --> 00:08:29.310
ordinary activity from an extreme event remains unknown.

